{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets","id":175941,"title":"[Question] On installing gadgets.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-21T05:56:58-07:00","id":175941,"title":"[Question] On installing gadgets.","content":"My players noticed something a little bit off about creating gadgets. In the Demon: The Descent book it states that, &quot;... the creator must expend a dot of Willpower to cement the gadget into reality. Should he fail to do so, the Installed power will wither away, vanishing by the end of the scene.&quot; This would be simple enough if not for the fact that on the later pages under pacts, that a Soul Pact requires a willpower dot expenditure also. However the book goes into far greater depth with the concept of spending a willpower dot here.<br /> <br /> Another problem is that the creation of a gadget costing a willpower dot doesn't seem to differentiate between Embedded or Exploited gadgets. RAW it seems to suggest that all gadgets cost the expenditure of a willpower dot (which the player will then have to restore with 1 experience). This seems awkward when you're getting a lesser form of an ability that you already possess. Granted it is now portable and reliable (and in the case of an Exploited Gadget it is no longer a compromise roll) but that only seems to be a &quot;good deal&quot; with Exploited gadgets, and very hit-and-miss with Embedded gadgets (as they offer very little risk in their use already).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? At current I've house-ruled that it was the expenditure of a willpower <b>point</b>. But... I'm not even sure I am entirely comfortable with that (as the only gadget that has been made was Exploited and I believe <i>that </i> might be worth the final cost of 1 willpower = 1 experience.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T00:13:40-07:00","id":176799,"title":"","content":"Err, what does that have to do with anything? Gadgets work for everyone, and are permanent, you make it essentially free to make and there will be nothing stopping your players from trading gadgets and hence collecting powers like they're pokemon. <br /> <br /> Or you know, since demons can easily have cults, you're begging for a demon then to equip his cult with numerous supernatural powers until they can just zerg rush any angel that comes sniffing by. <br /> <br /> Now maybe you're players are too nice for that, but with rules like that you're leaving your game open to being wrecked to fix what seems like a nonexistent problem. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T07:32:23-07:00","id":176983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets#post175941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Any thoughts? At current I've house-ruled that it was the expenditure of a willpower <b>point</b>. But... I'm not even sure I am entirely comfortable with that (as the only gadget that has been made was Exploited and I believe <i>that </i> might be worth the final cost of 1 willpower = 1 experience.)</div> </div> </div> </div> Like StSword said: the cost is there for game play balance reasons. Looking at all the other game lines this has been a consistent balancing issue for a long time, which is why it doesn't get explained on a metaphysical level. WW/OPP has been glossing over this thing for a long time now. Again, the difference between Embedded and Exploited is because of balancing issues. Under the current rules you could have a small hoard of cultists all armed with powerful Exploited Gadgets. It would require a gargantuan investment of willpower from a large ring of demons and then the weapons would just break down fairly quickly with no realistic means of keeping them all fueled with Aether. You could have an exciting few weeks of fairly high-powered urban warfare in the meanwhile, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2648-telperionst","name":"TelperionST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2648_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T08:35:14-07:00","id":177071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TelperionST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=176983#post176983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like StSword said: the cost is there for game play balance reasons. Looking at all the other game lines this has been a consistent balancing issue for a long time, which is why it doesn't get explained on a metaphysical level. WW/OPP has been glossing over this thing for a long time now. Again, the difference between Embedded and Exploited is because of balancing issues. Under the current rules you could have a small hoard of cultists all armed with powerful Exploited Gadgets. It would require a gargantuan investment of willpower from a large ring of demons and then the weapons would just break down fairly quickly with no realistic means of keeping them all fueled with Aether. You could have an exciting few weeks of fairly high-powered urban warfare in the meanwhile, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my current &quot;issue&quot; (and it's mostly academic) is that there is <i>no difference </i>between an Embedded Gadget and an Exploited Gadget. I'd have thought that an Embedded Gadget (since it has to be a <i>lesser</i> effect) would be cheaper than an Exploited Gadget.<br /> <br /> But I realised there was a problem with this logic: First that many of the embeds (Merciless Gunman anyone?) can be very powerful that even a <i>lesser</i> derivative effect could be quite potent. (I'm thinking clothes installed with Just Bruised.) The second is that there is no difference in the experience cost between an Embed or an Exploit, the difference is that an Exploit requires an Embed to be purchased. (Which wouldn't be translatable into gadget rules, nor should it be, really.) So, in the end, the Willpower <i>dot</i> is there to effectively place a cost on the gadget in experience. (1 Experience = 1 Willpower dot restored).<br /> <br /> The earliest part of my original post however was referring to the fact that under Pacts, which is after Gadgets, they make special reiteration for the expenditure of a willpower dot while the gadget rules just brush it off matter-of-factly. It felt strange to read. I have returned to RAW in my game (but allowed the player who made one gadget to not worry about the cost and just chop it up to experimenting with the systems <i>this time</i>). Nobody in my group seems to have a problem with this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T10:19:04-07:00","id":177152,"title":"","content":"I'd wait for <i>Flowers of Hell</i> to come out. They've said they expound upon Gadgets and stuff in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T23:31:53-07:00","id":177714,"title":"","content":"Well, embedded gadgets do have some advantages over exploit gadgets:<br /> <br /> Permanent without the required maintenance that exploit gadgets require.<br /> <br /> Retain their original looks, so they're stealthier. A supergun with merciless gunman looks normal, a demonic flamethrower with hellfire not so much.<br /> <br /> And exploit gadgets usually lose their original function in the transformation, a dagger with hush is still good at stabbing people, but a dagger with disintegrate might be less useful than a butter knife against an organic target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T06:15:16-07:00","id":177872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=177071#post177071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, my current &quot;issue&quot; (and it's mostly academic) is that there is <i>no difference </i>between an Embedded Gadget and an Exploited Gadget. I'd have thought that an Embedded Gadget (since it has to be a <i>lesser</i> effect) would be cheaper than an Exploited Gadget.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, there's a big difference. Exploited Gadgets are obviously something super-high magi-tech. Installing Hellfire in a gun turns it into a phaser out of Star Trek or some other sci-fi show. <br /> <br /> Exploited gadgets also leak aether, if memory serves - you stand out like a beacon to other demons or to cryptids who sense aether. Problematic in a game where you're primarily a spy. That cryptid guard dog could alert a guardian angel watching over the site you're investigating.... Or, hells, just alert a random cultist, who then causes a Compromise in you, which could send up a Flag on that Cover...<br /> <br /> <br /> In short - embeds are sneakier, and that's critical in a game where you need to be a spy. Demons seem very powerful with their more &quot;vulgar&quot; abilities, but those same abilities come with a huge risk. Being vulgar in Demon is very bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T10:53:12-07:00","id":178067,"title":"","content":"They <i>can </i>be detected by Aetheric resonance and do look overtly supernatural, this is very true, which gives them inherent disadvantages. (They'd be a compromise if witnessed by just about anyone.) But they are themselves not detectable by Angels until they've been destroyed. So if the object is well hidden and the angel isn't <i>looking </i>for it, it's unlikely to cause compromise.<br /> <br /> That said, I totally get what you guys are saying and can certainly see the pros and cons here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T13:53:51-07:00","id":178228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=178067#post178067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They <i>can </i>be detected by Aetheric resonance and do look overtly supernatural, this is very true, which gives them inherent disadvantages. (They'd be a compromise if witnessed by just about anyone.) But they are themselves not detectable by Angels until they've been destroyed. So if the object is well hidden and the angel isn't <i>looking </i>for it, it's unlikely to cause compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div> Angels? Correct, they cannot sense them. Cultists with Unseen Senses? Cryptids, especially the examples in the core book? Rogue demon operatives? All bets are off.<br /> <br /> Angels are not the only antagonist out there. They're the main ones, yes, but they're not alone. And, nine times out of ten, they're not the front line either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T20:44:23-07:00","id":178593,"title":"","content":"I had completely forgotten about other demons and cryptids in respect to gadgets! That actually adds an interesting potential to my player's gadget, as it is exploited and designed to garner his character pacts by being unleashed in &quot;the wild&quot; to find the right sort of person. Though I'm unsure how a cultist with Unseen Sense: God-Machine could find a source of aether, unless you suggest a God-Machine cultist with Unseen Sense: Demons?<br /> <br /> This begs another question: Does Unseen Sense: God-Machine cover demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:35:52-07:00","id":181807,"title":"","content":"As written no but nothing stops muggles or stigmatics from having multiple versions of unseen senses.<br /> <br /> The guy with unseen senses: god-machine, angels, demons, and cryptids is going to be prepared.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you got flowers of hell yet, but I hope that near field effect or lambda gadgets makes you see embedded gadgets as more useful. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T09:19:44-07:00","id":182040,"title":"","content":"Oh, I already see that gadgets are very useful, StSword. That's why I posted here, as I was questioning my original ruling. The expenditure of a Willpower dot is usually in order to gain something permanent, which a gadget is. So it makes sense. As for embedded gadgets, they were potentially more useful than exploited gadgets already. The additions in <i>Flowers of Hell</i> are very interesting.<br /> <br /> Though they lead to yet another question! Read as written, that willpower dot has to be expended to make a grouping of one-use gadgets. However, a willpower dot isn't usually used for something that is impermanent, like a one-use item. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T11:54:03-07:00","id":182135,"title":"","content":"I personally wouldn't charge a Willpower dot for the one-offs, but the rules don't say anything about that in Flowers of Hell.<br /> <br /> I think the Aether cost for making batches is its own balance point, since aside from taking the risk by assuming full demonic form it's rather hard to come by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T04:54:34-07:00","id":182796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=181807#post181807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As written no but nothing stops muggles or stigmatics from having multiple versions of unseen senses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your interpretation of the merit, not hard fact; there's nothing that says that Unseen Senses (God Machine) can't ping demons or cryptids. <br /> <br /> Actually, I think the intent is that stigmatics can feel demons by default because I seem to recall there being mentions of needing to Spoof God Machine cultists. That wouldn't be necessary if they couldn't Unseen Sense a demon in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:50:59-07:00","id":184552,"title":"","content":"The god-machine is more than capable of giving out unseen senses, so of course it can give out demon hunting cultists unseen senses-demons.<br /> <br /> As for rule interpretation, &quot;You have a sixth sense for a type of supernatural creature, chosen when you buy the merit,&quot; seems pretty damn clear to me. <br /> <br /> Which means that if you have unseen senses vampire, you can sense vampire, it doesn't help you sense ghouls. If you have unseen senses werewolves, then it doesn't help you sense wolfblooded or spirits.<br /> <br /> So by the rules of the game, unseen senses-godmachine lets you sense the godmachine. If there are more than one godmachines running around, the merit would let them sense those as well, but demons, cryptids, or angels aren't god-machines. <br /> <br /> Now there is nothing in the rules against taking the merit for more broad categories. Unseen senses-faeries could probably pick up true fae, changelings, and even hobgoblins, so a character with unseen senses-Things of the God-Machine would pick up angels as well as infrastructure, maybe even cryptids and demons as well, but unseen senses-god-machine and unseen senses-Things of the god-machine are two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T01:47:15-07:00","id":184661,"title":"","content":"That doesn't make any sense. The Unseen Sense: God-Machine merit has a specific case-note on how a character purchasing this version of the merit can see the gears of the God-Machine. If all it could do was get creeped out by Infrastructure being nearby, and not angels, then it would be functionally useless as a merit and it would not require that additional notation. It seems fairly clear to me that the intent behind the Unseen Sense: God-Machine merit is that it allows you to get the creepy feeling when an angel is nearby, potentially being able to pinpoint who the angel is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T03:39:42-07:00","id":184713,"title":"","content":"According to Heirs to Hell, Unseen Sense: God-Machine does not allow the detection of demons, but allows Demon-blooded to sense and see through Infrastructure, recognize Linchpins (although they don't necessarily know that it is a Linchpin), and sense angelic Numina (Wits + Composure - angel's Rank to sense Numen within half a mile).<br /> <br /> I would assume the Merit does the same, or less, for mortals. So maybe everything it does for Demon-blooded except recognizing Linchpins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:11:25-07:00","id":184981,"title":"","content":"A very interesting observation, Penta. Given that one of the example Stigmatics in the main book is used in the Storyteller material at the back and she is constantly smashing the Linchpin of that infrastructure (she doesn't know why, she just knows she is compelled to smash that telephone) I'd be willing to bet that this is the same for anyone with Unseen Sense: God-Machine. So, it seems pretty clear then that it allows you to detect anything still connected to the God-Machine. So not demons, but angels, infrastructure, linchpins and <i>certain</i> cryptids at the storyteller's discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T04:19:52-07:00","id":185440,"title":"","content":"<b>Further observations:</b><br /> <br /> Characters with Unseen Sense: God Machine can feel and angel falling. (rulebook p. 39)<br /> <br /> Demons sometimes have to spoof characters with Unseen Sense: God Machine. (implied on rulebook p. 119)<br /> <br /> Everyone with a sense for the God-Machine's workings can under close inspection tell there is something fundamentally different about gadgets. (rulebook p. 187)<br /> <br /> Even demons with &quot;Sense the Angelic&quot; can only detect Numina, and not the angels themselves. (rulebook p. 198)<br /> Sensing angels is not mentioned in the Unseen Sense write-up of demonblooded. (heirs to hell p. 33)<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion:</b><br /> <br /> Based on these observations (and my previous one), I rule that Stigmatics cannot detect angels, only their numina. If it is necessary for the plot, you could always use the visions a Stigmatic suffers to make him find an angel. Also the game seems to be in conflict on whether character's with Unseen Sense: Godmachine can detect demons. Maybe Stigmatics can only detect Demons under specific conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T02:32:48-07:00","id":203667,"title":"","content":"Since <b>Flowers of Hell</b> has come up, I got an issue concerning Angelic Detection of gadgets:<br /> <br /> It is quite often stated that Angels cannot perceive Aether in any way, shape or form (the example given has been <i>using cryptic hounds to sniff out demons</i>). Yet they suddenly can now, as of <b>Flowers of Hell</b>, specifically, when performing Installations. How's that? I'm figuring the angel in question doesn't actually detects the Aether flare like a Demon's senses... but can rather attempt to track the source of the anomalies that producing gadgets entails. I'm thinking detective work.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T05:12:21-07:00","id":203745,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Angels can detect large quantities of Aether, such as when an Angel falls. So Aether flares during Gadget installation would also be fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T07:26:20-07:00","id":203827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div 