g Installations. How's that? I'm figuring the angel in question doesn't actually detects the Aether flare like a Demon's senses... but can rather attempt to track the source of the anomalies that producing gadgets entails. I'm thinking detective work.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/120937-mandatory-silly-questions?p=187605#post187605\">Answered this earlier.</a> tl;dr Installation is explicitly accompanied by SFX that anyone can notice, as you've guessed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T15:17:19-07:00","id":204307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=203827#post203827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it was the exact reference I remembered, but the sidebar on p.39 starts with mentioning that everyone touched by the God-Machine can sense it when an angel falls, including stigmatics, angels and demons.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, I meant p.39 of the Demon: the Descent rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 07-21-2014, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T16:51:46-07:00","id":204351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=204307#post204307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it was the exact reference I remembered, but the sidebar on p.39 starts with mentioning that everyone touched by the God-Machine can sense it when an angel falls, including stigmatics, angels and demons.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, I meant p.39 of the Demon: the Descent rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, what <i>happens</i> when an angel Falls, along with the peripheral elements that are also capable of detecting the phenomenon, would seem to suggest that the methods are similar to tracking Installation locations for anything that doesn't have access to Aetheric resonance.<br /> <br /> Though this does remind me that I should probably account for the side effects of Doctor Pyrite's third Interlock\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T00:16:19-07:00","id":204712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=184661#post184661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't make any sense. The Unseen Sense: God-Machine merit has a specific case-note on how a character purchasing this version of the merit can see the gears of the God-Machine. If all it could do was get creeped out by Infrastructure being nearby, and not angels, then it would be functionally useless as a merit and it would not require that additional notation. It seems fairly clear to me that the intent behind the Unseen Sense: God-Machine merit is that it allows you to get the creepy feeling when an angel is nearby, potentially being able to pinpoint who the angel is.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a group in GMC who use their unseen senses to collect and hack infrastructure, I very much doubt those muggles who can travel through time, teleport cross country, summon angels, and manipulate the weather among other techno-miracles feel real cheated by their merit purchase in between playing god. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T05:39:43-07:00","id":205962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/175941-question-on-installing-gadgets?p=204712#post204712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a group in GMC who use their unseen senses to collect and hack infrastructure, I very much doubt those muggles who can travel through time, teleport cross country, summon angels, and manipulate the weather among other techno-miracles feel real cheated by their merit purchase in between playing god.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right. Because while they're hacking that infrastructure, they get goosebumps when it's caretaker gets home.<br /> <br /> The Merit normally allows an individual an extra-sensory perception on a supernatural entity. (Example: Unseen Sense: Werewolves allows you to sense nearby werewolves.) However, it notes that in addition to the affects of the merit that are normally permitted, you can see normally hidden infrastructure, identify infrastructure and see the gears of the God-Machine. This note is in <i>addition</i> to the affects of the merit as normally given. So, the question is: What are you sensing?<br /> <br /> I can understand the argument for a demon, they've been disconnected, or a cryptid because they're not necessarily part of the Machine (on an intentional level). But an Angel is an integral part of the Machine - indeed, Angels are often infrastructure themselves - so it seems fairly clear then that Unseen Sense: God-Machine would allow you to sense nearby angels. Do remember that the merit does not allow you such accuracy as to necessarily pinpoint anything that might be hiding itself - such as with the Numina &quot;Mortal Mask&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: Demon-blooded can use this merit to actually identify details of an infrastructure outright such as the Linchpin. Normal stigmatic characters are at the mercy of the storyteller as to what triggers it (though given the Stigmatic in &quot;How an Angel Dies&quot; constantly breaks the linchpin of the floating bridge infrastructure, it seems she must get the heebiejeebies from it) and seeing past Concealment Infrastructure doesn't necessarily mean you can immediately identify it as something bizarre (it might still be disguised as a ordinary building, just one that is invisible to normal human eyes). However, again, angels <i>are </i>infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 07-23-2014, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T01:57:12-07:00","id":208015,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Oh noes, the guy who wants to be able to summon an angel to smite his enemies like something out of Death Note will actually have to work for it, I'm crying on the inside here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> As for unseen sense-god-machine, nothing in Heirs to Hell says that there are multiple versions In fact, if the writers intent was that &quot;sensing lynchpins and angelic numina&quot; was a super special aspect of being demonblooded and had nothing to do with how unseen sense-god-machine works for everyone else, the correct way to express that in the English language is &quot;Demonblooded characters all have unseen senses-god-machine. Demonblooded characters can also sense lynchpins and angelic numina,&quot; because if sensing angelic numina and lynchpins weren't part of unseen sense-GM then there is no reason to connect them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> For that matter, demons can see infrastructure for what it is ala unseen sense-god-machine, and they can't sense angels unless they activate aetheric resonance and the angel is manifesting, using a numina, or an influence. Which honestly is probably going to be most of the time because how often is an angel just going to be sitting in twilight, but sensing when an angel is doing something is different from sensing an angel outright. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Now if I were writing things I'd have thrown in influence use with what unseen sense can pick up if one is going to pick up numina use, but whatever. </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T03:55:25-07:00","id":208106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heirs to Hell pg. 30-31 Anyone with Unseen Sense: God-Machine, and therefore all demon-bloods, can recognize Infrastructure. A demon-blood with Infrastructure Proficiency, though, has an instinctive understanding of Infrastructure. </div> </div> </div>It's a merit they can take, not a static part of a Demon-Blooded's template, I apologise for the mistake, but there it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oh noes, the guy who wants to be able to summon an angel to smite his enemies like something out of Death Note will actually have to work for it, I'm crying on the inside here.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I have no idea what this statement means or is in reference to or why it is relevant to the affects of Unseen Sense: God-Machine and how it may or may not allow a character to detect the presence of angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For that matter, demons can see infrastructure for what it is ala unseen sense-god-machine, and they can't sense angels unless they activate aetheric resonance and the angel is manifesting, using a numina, or an influence. Which honestly is probably going to be most of the time because how often is an angel just going to be sitting in twilight, but sensing when an angel is doing something is different from sensing an angel outright. </div> </div> </div>Demons do not have Unseen Sense: God-Machine as they are a major template and cannot normally acquire supernatural merits.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Angels are infrastructure. They are created by infrastructure - as most are - they are often maintained by other forces, such as cultists. Their mission is an occult matrix. The completion of which is the output the God-Machine desires. If you can use Unseen Sense: God-Machine to detect physical infrastructure why wouldn't you be getting the heebiejeebies from angels given that they are also infrastructure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}